---
description: Frontend standards for React/Next.js UI work
globs: ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.css", "src/app/**", "src/components/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Mobile-first: design at 375px, tap targets 44px or more, then scale up. Check 375, 768 and desktop before done.
- Every screen defines four states: loading, empty, error, success. No blank panels.
- One primary action per screen. Destructive actions need confirmation and look different.
- Forms: inline validation, keep input on error, disable submit while pending, every input labelled.
- TypeScript strict, no `any` without a comment. Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- Tailwind with shared tokens, no one-off magic numbers. Validate input with a zod schema shared with the backend.
- Semantic HTML, alt text, contrast 4.5:1, keyboard operable with visible focus.
- Format for South Africa: ZAR, `en-ZA`, explicit currency symbols.
- Pick a clear visual direction before building screens; avoid the default-template look. Real copy, not lorem ipsum.
- Budget: LCP under 2.5s on mid-range phone over 4G; no dependency over ~50 KB gzipped without a reason.
